  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Integrated Multi-sectoral Humanitarian Assistance to Vulnerable Displaced Populations in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan is currently navigating a transitional phase marked by a complex interplay of factors. Despite efforts to implement the peace process, contend with economic challenges, and grapple with existing informal political structures, these endeavours fall short in adequately addressing humanitarian needs.This Action aims to prevent, reduce, and mitigate protection threats while addressing the humanitarian needs of displaced populations in South Sudan, particularly those affected by the Sudan crisis. It involves providing multi-sector lifesaving humanitarian assistance in a safe, dignified, accessible, and participatory manner, prioritizing the most vulnerable populations. Building on previous initiatives, IOM&apos;s strategy includes providing critical services such water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), Shelter-Non Food Items (S-NFI), core pipeline supplies, and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM). These efforts aim to improve living conditions and address immediate humanitarian concerns, ensuring a secure and dignified environment for those affected.</narrative>
  </description>
